This directory has files for the programs on harmonic maps.

The program uses the "hmatrix" library, which is probably not
installed by default. I was using version 0.16.0.6. You need to install 'cabal' as well as 'ghc', and then install hmatrix with
% cabal install hmatrix

The '.lhs' files are literate haskell, and can be compiled by running
pdflatex on them. The output is included here.

Top-level
------------------------------------------------------------
Examples.hs: Main file. Many examples of specific graphs coming from rational maps.
Julia.lhs: Examples where Julia set is the whole sphere

Utility
------------------------------------------------------------
Util.hs: random utility stubs.
CyclicList.hs: treating linked lists as cyclic lists
IMatrix.hs: Wrapper around the hmatrix library. Mainly to allow vectors of length 0.
Mappable.hs: Some utility type classes to allow various types of "application"
Permutation.hs: Computing with permutations

Graphs
------------------------------------------------------------
Graph.lhs: Internal representation of graphs
GraphMap.lhs: Representing maps between graphs
GraphIO.lhs: textual representation of graphs of various types
GraphCover.lhs: Covers of graphs
Circle.lhs: Special functions for the circle and maps to it

Computations
------------------------------------------------------------
Harmonic.lhs: Harmonic (spring-energy-minimizing) maps between graphs
Filling.lhs: Finding minimal strutch factors
OptFilling.lhs: A start on optimizing the filling energy by varying elastic weights
Torus.lhs: Compute shape of sphere with four marked points
